WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Our guiding case is u equal to
three, so the order is thirty six.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.100
Assume, for contradiction, that a
circulant Hadamard matrix of this

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.080
order exists. Its thirty six sign
coefficients are hypothetical.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.180
Their polynomial times its
star equals thirty six.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.340
Since four and nine are coprime,
the Chinese remainder theorem

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.400
identifies the thirty six cycle with
a four cycle times a nine cycle.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.280
Replace X by Z times P.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.620
Coefficient j moves to the
cell with row j modulo four

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.660
and column j modulo nine. This
reorganizes the same coefficients.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.720
These grid rows are not
rows of the original matrix.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.480
Collect each row of the
grid as a polynomial in P.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.420
Call them H zero through H three.
Each has nine sign coefficients.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:56.490
The original polynomial
becomes H zero plus Z H one

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:02.467
plus Z squared H two plus Z cubed H three.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:07.970
The fourth roots of unity respect
Z to the fourth equals one.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.580
At Z equal to one, all four parts add.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.000
At negative one, their signs alternate.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.240
At i, the real part is H zero minus H two,

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.873
and the imaginary part
is H one minus H three.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.040
The value at negative i
conjugates the coefficients,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.620
giving no independent fourth polynomial.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:36.180
Divide each evaluation by two,
and call the results c, d, and g.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:41.850
Dividing both a polynomial and its star
by two divides their product by four.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.430
Thus thirty six becomes nine.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.610
Each of c, d, and g times
its star equals nine.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:53.960
For Gaussian coefficients, star conjugates
coefficients and reverses powers of P.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.860
Why are there no fractions?
Fix one power of P.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:03.540
For c and d, its numerator
is a sum of four signs,

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:07.360
possibly with alternating
signs. That sum is even.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.400
For the real and imaginary parts of g,

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.520
each numerator is a difference
of two signs, also even.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.520
Therefore c and d have
integer coefficients,

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.900
and g has Gaussian integer coefficients.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.700
Now substitute any ninth
root of unity for P.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.220
Star becomes complex conjugation,

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.950
so the norm identity says the squared
absolute value of each output is nine.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.380
All three values lie on
the circle of radius three.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:42.370
These are output values; the permitted
inputs satisfy P to the ninth equals one.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:44.820
Their pictured positions are schematic.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:52.820
For general odd u, the same construction
gives norm u squared and output radius u.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:55.970
Return to u equal to three.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:01.340
We will compare the inputs one
and omega, a cube root of unity.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:04.720
Both are ninth roots.
The norm fixes distances;

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.180
next we want to compare
the changes in phase.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.210
Here is a preview of Node six.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:16.620
Further information from the original
signs will force one common rotation to

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.200
carry all three outputs at
one to their outputs at omega.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:25.480
The illustrated hundred and twenty degree
rotation uses schematic starting points,

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.460
not values from an actual order
thirty six Hadamard matrix. This

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.680
common rotation is a later conclusion,
not a consequence of the norm alone.
